# A volume labelled ILEX-ANSWERS (or ILEXANSWERS, the name a FAT volume can
# carry) is read at boot only (ilex-installer-answers-gate.service decides, once,
# after udev has settled). One that appears later is not read: this rule only
# has the helper say so, once, on the console and the serial port; it starts
# nothing and stops nothing. The label is read by udev's blkid probe
# (60-persistent-storage.rules runs first).
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="block", ENV{ID_FS_LABEL}=="ILEX-ANSWERS|ILEXANSWERS", TAG+="systemd", ENV{SYSTEMD_WANTS}+="ilex-installer-answers-late@%k.service"
